	"printer_model": "FlashForge Creator 4",
	"printer_notes": "Creator 4, right extruder (T0) only -- the left IDEX head is deliberately kept off via M104 S0 T1 / M107 T1 in the start gcode, this profile does not drive it. IMPORTANT (confirmed via a real failed print, Aug 2026): use_relative_e_distances must be 0 (absolute E). A real FlashPrint export never uses M82/M83 and its E values climb continuously (absolute) -- an earlier version of this profile had use_relative_e_distances=1, which caused OrcaSlicer to emit M83 + small relative E deltas per move; the printer's right extruder never extruded (no motor activity at all) on a real test print using that version. Companion fix: before_layer_change_gcode's \"G92 E0\" is commented out -- OrcaSlicer itself flags this as incompatible with absolute extruder addressing (G92 E0 desyncs the printer's E position from what the slicer thinks it is). Do not re-enable relative E or uncomment G92 E0 without re-testing on real hardware. This profile ships a material-neutral baseline: M652 (case fan OFF) + M653 S0 / M656 S0 (chamber heat OFF). Select a matching filament profile (Generic PLA / Generic ABS @FlashForge Creator 4) to layer material-specific behavior on top via that profile's Filament Start G-code -- M651 Sxxx turns the case fan ON to speed xxx (0-255), M653/M656 set a chamber heater target (deg C) and (probably) a pre-heat timeout in seconds; confirmed against two real FlashPrint exports where ABS used fan-off+chamber-heat and PLA used fan-on+no-chamber-heat. See project README.md 'Filament profiles'. Remaining open questions, see README.md 'Open Questions': (1) bed origin -- this profile uses centered coordinates (-200,-175)-(200,175), inferred from real gcode coordinates for a small centered part, not yet confirmed against a full-bed print; (2) a trailing byte in the .gx binary header (0 vs 257 in two real samples, meaning unknown, likely cosmetic, not currently adjusted for filament-level fan overrides).",
